<Positioned left="510" top="224.94"><Text fontSize="26" color="#2DD4BFFF" fontFamily="Noto Sans Mono CJK SC" fontStyle="BOLD">02</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="552" top="228.94"><Text fontSize="12" color="#8FA0BCFF" fontFamily="Noto Sans Mono CJK SC" fontStyle="BOLD" letterSpacing="1">June–August</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="510" top="260.94"><Text fontSize="20" color="#F5F8FCFF" fontFamily="Inter" fontStyle="BOLD">On the cloud surface</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="510" top="286.94"><Text fontSize="13" color="#2DD4BFFF" fontFamily="Noto Sans Mono CJK SC" fontStyle="BOLD">Reservoirs become reactive</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="510" top="313"><Text fontSize="13" color="#B9C7DE" fontFamily="Noto Sans CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">Stable chlorine reservoirs — hydrochloric acid</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="510" top="331"><Text fontSize="13" color="#B9C7DE" fontFamily="Noto Sans CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">and chlorine nitrate — meet the surface of polar</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="510" top="349"><Text fontSize="13" color="#B9C7DE" fontFamily="Noto Sans CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">stratospheric cloud particles. Reactions there</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="510" top="367"><Text fontSize="13" color="#B9C7DE" fontFamily="Noto Sans CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">convert them into reactive forms such as Cl₂.</Text></Positioned>
